{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774368505,"nonce":"E+PKf4oCiis97V+TkfrOJ8gaIeQ=","title":"Checkpoints not unique per run — collisions in shared checkpoint directory","message":"## Summary\n\nCheckpoint files are named ckpt_{batch_number}.eqx in a shared directory (/tmp/feedbax-checkpoints/). Multiple training runs use the same directory and same naming scheme, so checkpoints from different runs overwrite each other. last_batch.txt also collides.\n\n## Impact\n\n- Running two experiments sequentially leaves stale checkpoints from run 1 that get mixed with run 2 checkpoints\n- SCP-ing checkpoints between machines (TPU→local) can overwrite local checkpoints with remote ones at the same batch number\n- No way to tell which run a checkpoint belongs to after the fact\n\n## Proposed fix\n\nInclude a run identifier in the checkpoint path. Options:\n1. Hash of the training config: ckpt_{config_hash}_{batch}.eqx\n2. Timestamp: ckpt_{timestamp}_{batch}.eqx\n3. User-specified run name: checkpoint dir per run (e.g., /tmp/feedbax-checkpoints/{run_name}/)\n\nOption 3 is simplest and most explicit. The TaskTrainer already has a chkpt_dir parameter — the training script should set it to a run-specific path.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e","files":null}]}